; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Mice Pursuit
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     pursuit curve, several turtles, towards, ask, simulation
; SUMMARY:  Puts a turtle on each corner of a polygon, each chasing the next one, and their paths spiral into the middle.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   This is the old "mice problem". Some mice sit on the corners of a
;   square. At the same moment each one starts running straight at
;   the next mouse round. But that mouse is moving too, so every mouse
;   keeps changing direction, and all of them spiral into the center
;   where they meet. Each mouse is a real turtle, leaving a colored
;   trail. Every few steps the program also joins the mice with thin
;   lines, which makes a whirl of shrinking, turning polygons.
;   It plays the chase for 3, 4, 5 and 6 mice, again and again.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch. Press Stop to end. Change STEP to make the
;   mice faster, or EVERY to draw the joining lines more or less often.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * several turtles: TELL, ASK and SETTURTLE
;   * TOWARDS gives the heading that points at a place
;   * updating all at once: first read every position, then move
;   * a pursuit curve: a path that keeps aiming at a moving target
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make one mouse slower than the others. Do they still meet?
;   * Start the mice at random places instead of on a polygon.
;   * For a square of side s, each mouse runs exactly s before they
;     meet. Measure it: count the steps.
; ============================================================

make "step 3
make "every 6
make "colors [[230 60 60] [240 170 30] [60 160 80] [50 110 220] [160 70 190] [30 170 180]]

; Put mice 0 .. n-1 on the corners of a polygon, all facing the middle.
to setup :n
  clean
  for [i 0 :n - 1] [
    ask :i [
      penup
      setxy 260 * sin 360 * :i / :n 260 * cos 360 * :i / :n
      setpencolor item :i + 1 :colors setpensize 2
      setshape "circle showturtle
      pendown
    ]
  ]
end

; Draw thin lines joining the mice, using a spare turtle that is
; never seen. Its number is n, one more than the last mouse.
to joinmice :n :spots
  ask :n [
    hideturtle penup setpencolor [170 170 190] setpensize 1
    setpos last :spots pendown
    foreach :spots [setpos ?]
    penup
  ]
end

to chase :n
  setup :n
  localmake "count 0
  forever [
    ; everybody's position first, so nobody moves before we have looked
    localmake "spots map [ask ? [pos]] iseq 0 :n - 1
    if (distancebetween first :spots item 2 :spots) < :step [
      ; they have met: hide the mice and stop
      for [i 0 :n] [ask :i [hideturtle]]
      stop
    ]
    if 0 = remainder :count :every [joinmice :n :spots]
    for [i 0 :n - 1] [
      ; mouse i runs toward the position of mouse i + 1 (the last chases the first)
      localmake "target item 1 + remainder :i + 1 :n :spots
      ask :i [setheading towards :target forward :step]
    ]
    make "count :count + 1
    wait 1
  ]
end

to distancebetween :a :b
  output sqrt ((first :a) - (first :b)) * ((first :a) - (first :b)) + ((last :a) - (last :b)) * ((last :a) - (last :b))
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 250 245]
forever [
  foreach [3 4 5 6] [
    chase ?
    wait 60
  ]
]
